+## Implemented mapping, 2026-10-08
+
+The [diagnostic ABI](/home/user/EDA-202/zhuowenjun/Workspace/Laya/LLAMA-HLS/Laya-baseline/results/attention_rtl_repair_20261008/d2_attention_preloaded/source/attention_preloaded_abi.h) fixes the 160-word descriptor layout, little-endian digest serialization and diagnostic E_PROTOCOL reasons. The [two-call top](/home/user/EDA-202/zhuowenjun/Workspace/Laya/LLAMA-HLS/Laya-baseline/results/attention_rtl_repair_20261008/d2_attention_preloaded/source/attention_preloaded_slice.cpp) holds one static runtime and import ticket; BEGIN uses the included production Controller::fresh plus parse/claim, while RUN validates the receipt, calls production row coverage/publish, then executes actual LOAD_KV, QK, inplace SCORE→PROB, Softmax and AV tasks. It reads ATT_OUT back into observed[144:208], records TaskDone and owner state in observed[0:16,224:238], and uses Controller::invalidate_incomplete on failed imports/tasks and after a successful partial-output test. No custom RTL exists in `rtl/`; generated RTL remains gated.
+
+The [independent fixture generator](/home/user/EDA-202/zhuowenjun/Workspace/Laya/LLAMA-HLS/Laya-baseline/results/attention_rtl_repair_20261008/d2_attention_preloaded/tb/generate_preloaded_fixture.py) creates physical-image hashes, three independent S64 gold cases, and the exact first BEGIN/RUN descriptor pages. The [CPU testbench](/home/user/EDA-202/zhuowenjun/Workspace/Laya/LLAMA-HLS/Laya-baseline/results/attention_rtl_repair_20261008/d2_attention_preloaded/tb/test_attention_preloaded.cpp) performs external `qkv_address`/`full_write` producer activity, then checks all 12 MiB of each returned host shard through the inverse formula before and after RUN. It compares the actual hash to the independently generated expected prefix and full-host hashes. The [CPU runner](/home/user/EDA-202/zhuowenjun/Workspace/Laya/LLAMA-HLS/Laya-baseline/results/attention_rtl_repair_20261008/d2_attention_preloaded/source/run_preloaded_cpu.py) links the official 24 production TUs plus this wrapper, with the controller included only once.
